I built the sprint board in plain TypeScript, and both commands pass: `./check` is clean and `./test` passes all 26 visible tests (3 of the 15 runs used). The code is in `src/main.ts` (the tabs), `src/board.ts`, `src/archive.ts` and `src/dom.ts`, all under `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/board-vanilla-opus-5/src/`. Every change shows at once. The page keeps the server's last confirmed state and redraws it with the unanswered actions on top, so a declined action undoes only itself without touching others still waiting; replies to a page you have left, or to an outdated column or checklist load, are ignored.

The brief left some choices open, and I made these:
- `left`/`right` are disabled while the target column is still loading or failed.
- A card still being added has no move buttons, sits below the real cards, and counts in To do's heading number.
- A loaded checklist resets that card's `<done>/<total>` on the board to match its items.
- Rename does not empty `title-input` afterwards, since the brief only says that for the add inputs.
- Titles and item text are trimmed, so input that is only spaces does nothing.
- I added retry buttons for a failed checklist and a failed archive list; the brief didn't ask for them.